&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer at Netlify, you&#39;ll join a collaborative team that values continuous learning, mutual support, and shared growth. Together, we create tools that help developers build faster, more intuitively, and with greater impact. Our Experience team owns the core product experience at Netlify, which is every way a human or an agent interacts with the platform, from our React-based web application to CLI, MCP, SDK, and API. If users interact with it directly, it&#39;s likely ours. We&#39;re reimagining how developers experience web development by thoughtfully integrating AI into our workflows - not as a novelty, but as a practical tool that enhances how we build the web.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With our team, you&#39;ll help set technical direction for our product area, mentor a highly senior team of engineers, and shape user experiences that serve millions of developers. You&#39;ll work closely with Product, Design, and engineering leadership, and partner with teams across the organization to build, iterate, and scale meaningful solutions. You&#39;ll have the autonomy to guide what we build and how, and the influence to bring others along with you, all while staying hands-on in the codebase.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for thoughtful engineers who enjoy owning problems end to end, collaborating across disciplines, and solving complex technical challenges for products that millions of developers rely on every day. AI is a foundational part of how we build, so we value engineers who are excited to thoughtfully incorporate AI-assisted workflows while continuing to apply strong engineering fundamentals. We believe the best engineering happens when talented people are trusted to solve difficult problems together, share what they&#39;re learning, and create space for different perspectives to shape better solutions.&amp;nbsp; With our team, you&#39;ll have real ownership from day one - not a tiny slice of a massive codebase. Engineers here are trusted to make decisions, shape technical direction, and move quickly while collaborating closely with Product and Design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use your deep expertise in full-stack development (TypeScript, JavaScript, Go, and React) to ship reliable, scalable, performant code across our product suite, and set the patterns that others on the team and across the org follow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical direction for our product area, including the web app, CLI, MCP, SDK, API, and docs, by defining architecture and roadmap alongside your manager, Product, and Design, and make tradeoffs explicit so decisions are easy to understand and revisit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead large, ambiguous projects that span multiple teams from conception to delivery, such as our application rewrite and upcoming CLI rework, writing RFCs, driving alignment, and managing risk and timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve user-facing features and product APIs for both humans and agents, recognizing that the best interface isn’t always a React application. Build them to scale to millions of developers worldwide, with a clear view of reliability, performance, and long-term maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make thoughtful product and interface decisions on your own with the overall customer experience top of mind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the bar for engineering practices - testing, documentation, observability, and performance optimization - and lead how the team pragmatically uses AI tools, sharing what works and what doesn&#39;t&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn ambiguity into clear plans, guiding both early-stage prototypes and production-ready applications that directly impact user experience and business metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and grow engineers through code reviews, design reviews, pairing, and sponsorship, raising the technical level of the whole team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practice proactive async communication and create visibility across projects by documenting your workflows and decision-making clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in on-call rotations, lead incident follow-up, and drive continuous improvement efforts that reduce technical debt and prevent recurring problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams and engineering leadership to shape user flows that enhance the developer experience across our platform, and contribute to hiring and team growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in TypeScript and JavaScript, with a long track record of designing, shipping, and maintaining production-quality software in modern full-stack environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of building interfaces developers use directly, such as web apps, CLIs, APIs, SDKs, or other dev tools, and a strong sense of what works well for developers (and, by extension, agents)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for building strong user-facing experiences, including working with React and modern frontend architecture and making architectural decisions that hold up as products and teams grow, paired with the backend knowledge to design software well beyond the UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product and design instincts. This isn’t about visual polish - it’s about making thoughtful decisions about how users interact with a product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with Go and/or Ruby for backend services and API development, with a thoughtful approach to reliability and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with React and modern frontend architecture, including making architectural decisions that hold up as products and teams grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to raise the technical bar: providing direction to senior and staff-level engineers, distributing ownership, mentoring, shaping standards, and influencing decisions beyond your own team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience delivering features and services that serve large user bases, including designing for scale and operating systems in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading technically complex, cross-team projects from ambiguous problem to shipped outcome, including writing RFCs and building consensus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to raise the technical bar: mentoring senior and mid-level engineers, shaping standards, and influencing decisions beyond your own team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing high-quality, testable code that&#39;s reliable and maintainable over time, and setting that expectation for others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency using and experimenting with AI-assisted development tools, with sound judgment about when and how to apply them and the ability to help others do the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to open-source projects or working in public codebases is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, especially in asynchronous, remote-first environments, with the ability to explain tradeoffs to engineers, leadership, and non-technical partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical thinking abilities and a solution-oriented approach to complex technical challenges, with the judgment to prioritize and say no when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach to problem-solving with curiosity about how your work supports teammates, users, and broader goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset and openness to learning new tools, technologies, and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for working in a collaborative environment with diverse teams across distributed locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Role is a Great Fit If&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re energized by building user-facing products and features that directly impact millions of developers&#39; daily workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in collaborative environments, working closely with your team and cross-functionally to turn ideas into reality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy the autonomy and influence of staff-level work - setting technical direction, writing RFCs, and driving decisions across teams while staying connected to the people doing the work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You find satisfaction in making other engineers better, whether through mentoring, design reviews, or setting a clear example&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You see ambiguity as a creative opportunity and can navigate uncertainty to build practical solutions and bring clarity to others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You see AI as a multiplier for your skills, not a shortcut, and can articulate where it helps, where it doesn&#39;t, and how you use it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re excited by new tools, challenges, and opportunities to grow, even when they feel a little uncomfortable at first&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to work on a fully remote team that believes in autonomy, transparency, and building a better web, together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applying&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet 100% of our qualifications? &lt;strong&gt;Please apply anyway!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When applying please include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A resume or short listing of your job history &amp;amp; skills (link to a LinkedIn profile would be fine). We appreciate a cover letter explaining why you would enjoy working in this role at Netlify to get to know you a bit better, though this is not required and will not impact your application. Our mission is to “build a better web” and that cannot be done without a diversity of skill sets, backgrounds and thoughts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Of everything we&#39;ve ever built at Netlify, we are most proud of our team. Netlify is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are devoted to building a team of people with diverse backgrounds and lifestyles. Driving equality empowers our team, enables us to innovate, and helps us maintain a more inclusive environment. We don’t discriminate against employees or applicants based on gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, age, race, military/veteran status, citizenship, pregnancy status, or any other differences. If we can do anything to provide a better interview, i.e. accommodate a disability, then please let us know by emailing accommodations@netlify.com.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Netlify&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify is a platform that lets you create, share, and run anything on the web: a website, an app, an agent experience, whatever you can dream up. Use your own tools or ours to build it, collaborate with your team, get it live, and keep it running. Anyone, from people just starting out to seasoned developers, can create pro-level web experiences that really work, really well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Series D company that has raised over $200M from investors such as Andreessen Horowitz, Kleiner Perkins, EQT, Bessemer, BOND, and Menlo Ventures. As a fully distributed company, we aim to create a company culture where the best idea can come from anywhere and strive to be thoughtful, compassionate, and collaborative in our work. If this sounds like something you’d like to be part of, we’re excited to connect with you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Netlify, we are committed to a compensation philosophy that prioritizes fairness and equity, positions our employee compensation competitively in the market, recognizes and rewards performance, and takes a comprehensive approach to our rewards package. We anchor our compensation philosophy on a market-based approach, therefore salary ranges may differ depending on the labor cost in a particular location. The salary provided is in addition to robust benefits and participation in Netlify’s equity plan. Our hiring range for this role is targeted at $182,000 - $248,000 for most US-based locations, $175,000 - $235,000 CAD in most Canada-based locations, and £105,000 – £144,000 GBP for most UK-based locations.&amp;nbsp; Candidates outside the US, Canada, UK, or in premium markets should consult with their Talent Acquisition partner regarding location-based ranges, as they may be higher or lower than the average US range listed. The starting pay will be determined based on multiple factors, including expertise and skills, market demands, experience, internal equity, and applicable geographic location. These compensation packages and ranges are subject to change and may be modified in the future.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flexport:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flexport, we believe global trade can move the human race forward. That’s why it’s our mission to make global commerce so easy there will be more of it. We’re shaping the future of a $10T industry with solutions powered by innovative technology and exceptional people. Today, companies of all sizes—from emerging brands to Fortune 500s—use Flexport technology to move more than $19B of merchandise across 112 countries a year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recent global supply chain crisis has put Flexport center stage as we continue to play a pivotal role in how goods move around the world. We are proud to have the support of the best investors in the game who believe in our mission, solutions and people. Ready to tackle global challenges that impact business, society, and the environment? Come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Customs Matters More Than Ever&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;International trade is under more pressure than ever before. With tariffs, shifting regulations, and geopolitical uncertainty, customs has gone from a back-office function to a boardroom priority. The recent trade crisis — sparked by Trump-era tariffs — has made customs the single most complex challenge for global businesses. For many, it’s the difference between keeping supply chains moving or grinding them to a halt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That’s where we come in. The &lt;strong&gt;Customs Technology team&lt;/strong&gt; at Flexport is leading the charge. We are building the systems that help entrepreneurs and global brands navigate complexity, stay compliant, and keep the world’s goods flowing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customs brokerage is one of the largest, most under-innovated opportunities in logistics. Legacy customs brokers are stuck with outdated systems and manual processes—they simply can’t adapt fast enough.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flexport is growing fast because we’re different. We are the only big tech company in the space, and the only freight forwarder that got founded after the launch of Netscape. Being a tech company, we can move much faster than our competitors, and give our customers the service they expect in this day and age. We can deploy things like LLM agents at scale, in an industry that is ripe to be disrupted by this technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager in the Customs Technology team, you’ll lead a group of exceptional engineers to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build world class tools like our Tariff Simulator, the only tool that gives businesses a real view of landed costs before they ship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate customs processes to an unprecedented level. Most customs are text based work, which is what agents excel at.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design scalable systems that automate classification, compliance, and filings—turning weeks of work into seconds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, design, and operations to deliver technology that gives clients clarity, cost savings, and risk control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and grow a world-class 8-10 member engineering team that thrives on solving the hardest problems in logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the future of customs into a transparent, efficient, and strategic advantage for businesses worldwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Things We ❤️&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leveraging AI in a safe way to eliminate mundane work for customs brokers and automate customs every step of the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modeling complex and ambiguous domains into fully automated workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building highly performant and reliable Kotlin services on our cutting-edge infrastructure platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with end users across the globe to create the best possible product: removing toil and surfacing interesting cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Should Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of experience leading software engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to break down complex problems into actionable plans. You need to go deep into details in a domain completely unfamiliar to you, and come out with an end to end understanding to automate it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Founder Mentality &amp;amp; Ownership: An entrepreneurial instinct. You operate like an owner, thrive in ambiguity, and take ideas from 0 to 1 without needing a predetermined playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A love of simple, well-tested code that is easy to extend and hard to break&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias for action — you see problems and solve them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An aptitude for learning quickly (non-optional)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The latest and greatest hardware and software to support you, including all AI tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile ways of working — without being tied to a single doctrine like Scrum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A modern stack: moving from a React/Flow + Ruby on Rails monolith to React/Typescript, Kotlin microservices on Kubernetes. We also use and love GraphQL, gRPC, Postgres, Kafka, and Snowflake.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in It for You?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An opportunity to contribute to one of the fastest-growing companies, with global impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily catered lunches (vegetarian options included), breakfast, snacks, coffee/tea and soft drinks in our office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Covered commute expenses for employees living outside Amsterdam&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 vacation days per year (full-time)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid health insurance (basic and additional packages) through a collective plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A defined pension contribution scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity program: become a shareholder in a multi-trillion-dollar industry disruptor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program (Aetna Resources for Living)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental leave benefit for both mothers and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;1704749847.557549&quot; class=&quot;c-virtual_list__item&quot; data-qa=&quot;virtual-list-item&quot; data-item-key=&quot;1704749847.557549&quot;&gt;
